{"id":1671,"date":"2026-08-24T03:51:15","date_gmt":"2026-08-24T03:51:15","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/?post_type=knowledgebase&#038;p=1671"},"modified":"2026-08-24T04:24:10","modified_gmt":"2026-08-24T04:24:10","slug":"export-as-xps","status":"publish","type":"knowledgebase","link":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/db\/export-share\/export-as-xps\/","title":{"rendered":"Export as XPS"},"content":{"rendered":"<div style=\"color: #2b2b2b;\">\n<h2 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">Export as XPS<br \/>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1680\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/ExportAsXPS.webp\" alt=\"Export as XPS\" width=\"112\" height=\"110\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/ExportAsXPS.webp 960w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/ExportAsXPS-300x296.webp 300w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/ExportAsXPS-768x758.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 112px) 100vw, 112px\" \/><\/span><\/h2>\n<p class=\"western\">For Windows users or corporate environments where PDF is not supported, Open Publisher can produce an <strong>XPS (XML Paper Specification)<\/strong> file &#8211; Microsoft&#8217;s built-in alternative to PDF. XPS files work natively on virtually any Windows machine without requiring Adobe Acrobat or any third-party software.<\/p>\n<div style=\"background-color: #f2f2f2; padding: 10px; margin-bottom: 20px; border-left: 4px solid #007670;\">\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Note:<\/strong> Because XPS is a proprietary Microsoft format, this export method relies on the Windows operating system. macOS and Linux users will not have access to the XPS Document Writer in their native print dialogs.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/div>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">How to Export as XPS<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1674\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-24-045017.png\" alt=\"Export as XPS\" width=\"533\" height=\"233\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-24-045017.png 1376w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-24-045017-300x131.png 300w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-24-045017-1024x447.png 1024w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/Screenshot-2026-08-24-045017-768x335.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 533px) 100vw, 533px\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">Click <strong>Export XPS<\/strong> in the <strong>File<\/strong> or <strong>Home<\/strong> ribbon tab (next to the PDF export button).<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">A dialog opens explaining the process. Because web browsers cannot natively generate XPS files on their own, the button hooks into your browser&#8217;s native print engine and instructs you to select <strong>\u201cMicrosoft XPS Document Writer\u201d<\/strong> as your printer destination.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\">When the print dialog opens, confirm that <strong>Microsoft XPS Document Writer<\/strong> is selected as the printer destination. Click <strong>Print<\/strong>, choose a destination folder on your computer, enter a file name, and click <strong>Save<\/strong>.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<h3 class=\"western\"><span style=\"color: #007670;\">Troubleshooting<img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignright wp-image-1678\" src=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/XpsTroubleshooting.webp\" alt=\"Troubleshooting\" width=\"152\" height=\"159\" srcset=\"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/XpsTroubleshooting.webp 427w, http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/08\/XpsTroubleshooting-287x300.webp 287w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 152px) 100vw, 152px\" \/><\/span><\/h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Missing XPS Document Writer:<\/strong> If this option does not appear in your printer list, it may be disabled on your machine. Go to <strong>Windows Settings &gt; Apps &gt; Optional Features<\/strong>, click &#8220;Add a feature,&#8221; and install the Microsoft XPS Document Writer.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<li>\n<p align=\"left\"><span style=\"font-size: small;\"><strong>Print Dialog Blocked:<\/strong> If clicking the export button does nothing, ensure your web browser&#8217;s pop-up blocker is not preventing the print dialog from launching. Look for a blocked pop-up icon in your URL address bar.<\/span><\/p>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Export as XPS For Windows users or corporate environments where PDF is not supported, Open Publisher can produce an XPS (XML Paper Specification) file &#8211; Microsoft&#8217;s built-in alternative to PDF. XPS files work natively on virtually any Windows machine without requiring Adobe Acrobat or any third-party software. Note: Because XPS is a proprietary Microsoft format, [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1680,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","template":"","knowledgebase_cat":[21],"class_list":["post-1671","knowledgebase","type-knowledgebase","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","knowledgebase_cat-export-share"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/1671","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase"}],"about":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/knowledgebase"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=1671"}],"version-history":[{"count":11,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/1671\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1689,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase\/1671\/revisions\/1689"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1680"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1671"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"knowledgebase_cat","embeddable":true,"href":"http:\/\/acr.floydcraft.co.uk\/openpublisher\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/knowledgebase_cat?post=1671"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}